Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
- Reuse SnoozeMenuButton before Settle in folder and folder-multiline hover actions, with the existing availability gate, presets, custom dialog, environment and open-state handling.
- When Snooze is shown, stack the time label and the Snooze/Settle controls in one grid cell so the status slot always reserves the wider of the two; hover, keyboard focus and the open menu only swap opacity, so long titles truncate at the same point at rest and on hover. Woke rows keep the label beside the controls. Preserve Woke presentation. Without Snooze, keep the upstream Settle overlay and its Woke behavior. Keep controls available while the menu is open and suppress the enclosing details tooltip.
- Keep Snooze out of settled/snoozed slim rows. Preserve card rows, settle/unsettle actions and snoozed/Woke status decisions. Web, desktop renderer and mobile browser share these row variants; native mobile, server and providers are unchanged.

Integration details:
- Preserve upstream grouped Settle tooltips, jump-hint status slot/badge, rem-based row heights and button keyboard accessibility.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Applied without conflicts. On 965ddc1d6c folder and folder-multiline rows still offer only Settle (SidebarThreadRow.tsx did not change upstream), so grouped Snooze still needs this commit.

Port to ee4ef06469:
- The hover test finds the title as the innermost span holding its text: upstream #25269 removed aria-hidden from the title span and its screen-reader copy, so the old span[aria-hidden] lookup found nothing.

Port to fe59fa44d0: the folder row details tooltip now reads disabled={isRenaming || snoozeMenuOpen || sortable?.isDragging}, keeping the rename suppression upstream #31009 added next to the open-menu suppression, in the order upstream uses on the other row variant.

Port to b6ac2449f1: the Snooze and Settle hover branch keeps this commit's structure under upstream's translated labels (055b44919e): gt() aria labels and <T> tooltips, English unchanged.

Port to b8be2287dc: upstream 78de041d48 (#24917, settle and snooze threads while their machine is offline) gates the row's Snooze on canTriageThread (operate scope not denied) instead of canOperateThread and shows a Pending label while a triage change waits to sync. The grouped Snooze keeps this commit's slim-row exclusion on top of upstream's new gate, so folder and folder-multiline rows offer Snooze offline exactly when card rows do; the stacked label cell holds upstream's Pending label in place of the time label. Upstream still offers only Settle in grouped rows, so this commit is still needed.

Port to 0085217d1b: SidebarThreadRow.tsx follows upstream ea3328c50c (#42671, one shared tooltip serves every trigger): the folder and slim row is now a ThreadHoverCardTrigger, which takes this commit's snoozeMenuOpen in its disabled condition, and the Un-settle and Settle buttons, including the Settle button beside the snooze menu, are SharedTooltipTrigger with a label instead of Tooltip, TooltipTrigger and TooltipPopup. The layout, the slim-row rule and the snooze menu are unchanged.

